statement:
You get an integer array `arr` and three limits `a`, `b` and `c`. Count the index triples `i < j < k` for which all three of these hold:

- `arr[i]` and `arr[j]` differ by at most `a`;
- `arr[j]` and `arr[k]` differ by at most `b`;
- `arr[i]` and `arr[k]` differ by at most `c`.

"Differ by at most x" means the absolute value of the difference is no more than x. Return how many such triples exist.

validator:
function validate([arr, a, b, c]) {
  if (!Array.isArray(arr) || arr.length < 3 || arr.length > 100) return 'arr needs 3 to 100 values.';
  if (arr.some(v => !Number.isInteger(v) || v < 0 || v > 1000)) return 'Each value of arr is an integer from 0 to 1000.';
  for (const limit of [a, b, c]) if (!Number.isInteger(limit) || limit < 0 || limit > 1000) return 'a, b and c are integers from 0 to 1000.';
  return null;
}

